# CODEOWNERS — promotion authority, made mechanical (ADR-0004).
#
# A change to the methodology's promotion-sensitive surfaces requires an admin
# review before it can merge (paired with the `pull_request` ruleset's
# require_code_owner_review — see docs/governance/main-ruleset.json). This turns
# "who may change the methodology" from one operator's unilateral judgment over a
# manual grep (charter risk #6) into a structural gate.
#
# KNOWN DEGRADE (not a bug): while the admin set is a single person, GitHub does
# not require review from a PR's own author, so this collapses to a self-approval
# no-op. The model is correct but only BINDS once a second admin joins — matching
# the charter's "ratified by the first non-Nino consumer" gate. When this repo
# moves under an org, replace `@nino-chavez` with `@<org>/blueprint-admins` (the
# `access.roles.admin` team) and the gate binds automatically.

# The methodology itself — first principles, taxonomies, ADRs.
/METHODOLOGY.md            @nino-chavez
/docs/                     @nino-chavez

# The substrate every consumer stamps from.
/template/                 @nino-chavez

# Amendment ledgers (promotion candidates) anywhere in the tree.
*AMENDMENTS*               @nino-chavez

# Governance + distribution config — changing the rules needs an admin.
/.github/                  @nino-chavez
/CONTRIBUTING.md           @nino-chavez
/consumers.yml             @nino-chavez
/package.json              @nino-chavez
